APPENDIX C - effective significance level of the shipped FR50 test

================================================================================

Because the Gumbel tail is thin, inflating the threshold by 1/c = 1.2533 costs

~3 orders of magnitude in LEVEL, not 25%. alpha_eff = 1 - exp(-exp(-x)) where

x = (thr_shipped - a_n) / b_n, i.e. the shipped threshold re-expressed as a

Gumbel quantile of the statistic's own null max distribution.



n_obs      a_n     b_n   thr_shipped  thr_correct   effective_alpha   tighter_by

     2319  3.5313  0.2540      5.8903       4.6998         9.262e-05       108.0x   <- CT-3 window

   200000  4.5718  0.2024      6.8968       5.5029         1.026e-05       974.9x   <- per-symbol full history

 18781302  5.4453  0.1728      7.8208       6.2401         1.069e-06      9353.6x   <- whole corpus



Nominal alpha = 0.01 in all three rows. The per-symbol row is the

production-relevant one: extract_jumps computes its threshold from the count of

finite sigma-hat values for the symbol it is given (~214,650 bars for a

full-history symbol), so FR50 ships at an effective level near 1e-5.
